 <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 19:05:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] camera: zoom the viewfinder by pinch, scroll or double tap

The viewfinder had no zoom at all, which on a phone is the control people
reach for first: the rear sensor is far wider than the screen, so framing
anything at a distance meant walking closer.

Add digital zoom on camerabin's own `zoom` property rather than magnifying
the displayed paintable. camerabin crops in the source, through the
wrappercamerabinsrc that Aperture already installs, so the pictures and
videos that are saved are zoomed exactly as they were framed - a preview-only
zoom would quietly save a wider picture than the one the user composed.

Three ways in, because the app runs on both phones and desktops: a pinch
gesture, the scroll wheel, and a double tap that toggles between 1x and 2x.
The factor appears briefly over the viewfinder while it changes, and resets
to 1x when the camera is switched, since a zoom belongs to the sensor you
were pointing rather than to the app.

The range is camerabin's own: 1x to its max-zoom, which it reports as 10.
---
 aperture/src/viewfinder.rs  |  38 ++++++++++++
 data/resources/ui/camera.ui |  19 ++++++
 src/widgets/camera.rs       | 115 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 172 insertions(+)

